      contexto: 'Overtime is a structural component of the Montevideo city government\'s payroll, above all in street cleaning, lifeguarding, health clinics and social development. The rules set a monthly cap of 40 hours per employee. In 2025, fourteen opposition councillors on the Departmental Board gathered the one-third of votes the Constitution requires to ask the Court of Accounts for a specific audit of how those hours were authorised and paid during the previous administration. The request was approved on 31 July 2025 and the audited period runs from 26 November 2020 to 9 July 2025.',
